WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.060
Many upcoming high-profile films have already
scheduled their debuts, and some have even

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.000
released trailers to the public at large.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.860
Unfortunately, some of them also look pretty
lame.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.820
You heard it here first, these are fated to
be the worst movies of 2019.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.500
All the most popular stage musicals eventually
get adapted into films, they're well-known

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:25.539
enough for studios to take a chance on them,
they almost always score an Oscar nom or two,

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.860
and they give musical fans who don't live
in New York a rare chance to enjoy them.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.180
In 2019, another well-known musical will hit
movie screens.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.680
And no, sadly it’s not Hamilton.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:37.760
It’s Cats.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:43.980
Debuting on Broadway in 1982, Cats is a loosely
plotted show, based on a book of poetry by

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:44.480
T.S.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.100
Eliot, which is about, well… cats.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.980
Singing, dancing, frolicking, homeless cats.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.920
Cats's original run ended in 2000, and Hollywood
has finally figured out a way to do this show,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.460
but not via animation, like you might expect.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:03.440
No, it seems the stars of the movie, who include
Taylor Swift, Ian McKellen, Jennifer Hudson

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.860
and James Corden, are going to actually dress
up in cat costumes.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.260
So does this have any prayer of being the
next musical to clean up at the Oscars?

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.880
Not meow, not ever.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:19.320
It just wouldn't be a new year without another
movie in which an angry Liam Neeson tracks

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.980
and kills a small army of bad guys who did
him wrong.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.640
Following the three Taken movies, Run All
Night, The Commuter and many, many more, comes

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:28.580
Cold Pursuit.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:33.920
This time, Neeson shows off his very particular
set of skills as a mild-mannered Rocky Mountains

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:39.250
snow-plow driver named Nelson who is forced
into action when his son is killed by a drug

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:39.740
cartel.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:44.020
Unfortunately, Neeson has done this same movie
so many times that it's starting to get a

00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:45.110
little embarrassing.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:47.060
“Then why would I do it?”

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.920
“Because there would be a reward.”

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:53.640
“Uh-huh.”

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.020
One thing in Cold Pursuit's favor, however,
is that it's based on a pretty good Norwegian

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.980
dark comedy called In Order of Disappearance.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.100
It’s just a shame they seem to have drained
all the humor out of it.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.440
In The Beach Bum, the always cool and totally
chill Matthew McConaughey plays a beach-loving

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.740
stoner named Moondog.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.140
And no, despite what you might remember, this
movie doesn’t already exist.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.120
Maybe you’re thinking of Surfer, Dude?

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.960
“Is that a job, surfer?”

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.240
“Not really.”

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:29.060
While the title and details make it sound
like a straight-to-video, National Lampoon-branded

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:34.700
boorish comedy from the early '90s, it's actually
an indie movie, albeit one directed by Harmony

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.140
Korine, mostly known for more unsettling projects
such as Kids and Gummo.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.430
At least the cast is likable: Zac Efron plays
a dude named "Flicker," Snoop Dogg portrays

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:49.540
someone genuinely named "Lingerie," and Martin
Lawrence makes an appearance as "Captain Wack."

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.360
Roll on awards season.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.420
The Rambo movies may hold claim to the film
franchise that has veered the furthest from

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:57.500
its original intent.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:03.460
The first entry in the series, First Blood,
was the harrowing and tragic story of a PTSD-stricken

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:08.590
Vietnam War veteran, starring Sylvester Stallone
in what was probably his finest and most nuanced

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:10.040
work since the original Rocky.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.880
Then came the second one, and everything changed.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.180
"The war won't stop with First Blood Part
II.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.060
It will escalate to Rambo 3.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:21.140
Which should really be called Rambo 2 First
Blood Part 3, but the Rambo titles never made

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:21.640
sense."

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:26.680
The political climate of the 1980s fueled
an explosion of action movies that celebrated

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:31.460
American patriotism and hardcore violence,
and so the subsequent First Blood sequels

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:36.490
had that same broken man become a muscle-bound,
machine-gun wielding one-man army who routinely

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.820
shoots up entire villages full of terrorists.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:44.500
“Live for nothing or die for something.”

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:49.740
Stallone’s career has been reinvigorated
in recent years thanks to the success of old-school

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.380
action franchise The Expendables, as well
as his Oscar nomination for the role of Rocky

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.600
Balboa in Creed.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.840
As part of this victory lap, Stallone has
decided to go and make the completely unnecessary

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.740
Rambo 5.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.800
This time, Rambo faces off against a drug
cartel.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.240
Odds are, he'll come out on top, which is
an impressive feat considering both Stallone

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.920
and his character are well over 70 years old.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:17.520
The Rhythm Section is pretty much exactly
like Peppermint, 2018’s moderately successful

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.600
Taken rip-off starring Jennifer Garner.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.930
This one stars Gossip Girl veteran Blake Lively
as Stephanie Patrick, a woman who slowly and

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:29.410
methodically tracks down a bunch of bad guys
because she just knows they're responsible

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:31.420
for the plane crash that killed her family.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:36.560
Lively is no stranger to an action thriller,
having starred in 2016’s The Shallows, but

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.580
it’s hard to get worked up about this.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.660
And the best part?

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.900
It’s based on a book series, so you can
probably count on a sequel or six somewhere

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:44.800
down the line.

